cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  BeCoMe: a web application for best-compromise group decision
  making with fuzzy expert opinions
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below, and cite the
  paper that introduced the method it implements (listed under references).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kuzmina
    given-names: Ekaterina
    affiliation: >-
      Faculty of Economics and Management, Czech University of Life Sciences Prague
repository-code: https://github.com/caitlon/BeCoMe
license: PolyForm-Noncommercial-1.0.0
version: 1.0.0-beta.1
date-released: 2026-09-07
abstract: >-
  An independent implementation of the BeCoMe (Best-Compromise Mean) method for
  aggregating expert opinions expressed as fuzzy triangular numbers, extended into a
  working web application so people who do not write code can run a panel.
keywords:
  - group decision making
  - fuzzy numbers
  - best-compromise mean
  - multi-criteria decision analysis
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      BeCoMe: Easy-to-implement optimized method for best-compromise group decision
      making: Flood-prevention and COVID-19 case studies
    authors:
      - family-names: Vrana
        given-names: Ivan
      - family-names: Tyrychtr
        given-names: Jan
      - family-names: Pelikán
        given-names: Martin
    journal: Environmental Modelling & Software
    volume: 136
    start: 104953
    year: 2021
    doi: 10.1016/j.envsoft.2020.104953
